REQUIRES: xmake

%t sits inside catter's own configured build tree, and xmake prefers the
nearest configured project above the working directory, so every call pins
the project with -P.

xmake's build cache compiles in two steps, preprocessing each source first
(-E) and then compiling the preprocessed file; it is disabled here so the
entries come from the plain compile. xmake also compiles temporary files to
probe compiler flags during the build; those count as other entries.

RUN: %e2e prepare hello %t
RUN: cd %t && xmake config -P . --ccache=n --yes
RUN: cd %t && %catter script::cdb -q -o %t/compile_commands.json -- xmake build -P .
RUN: %e2e summarize %t/compile_commands.json %t | FileCheck %s

CHECK: entries: 2
CHECK-NEXT: other entries: {{[0-9]+}}
CHECK-NEXT: src/main.cc exists dir=. output=build/.objs/hello/{{.+}}/src/main.cc.{{o|obj}} define=yes
CHECK-NEXT: src/util.cc exists dir=. output=build/.objs/hello/{{.+}}/src/util.cc.{{o|obj}} define=yes
